; SELinux policy for httpdog. Needed where SELinux is enforcing: Fedora, RHEL, Rocky Linux, AlmaLinux.
;
; nginx runs in the httpd_t domain. httpdog has no domain of its own, so it runs in unconfined_service_t.
; Without this rule SELinux does not let nginx send its access log to httpdog's unix socket: no log line
; arrives, and nginx's error log shows "connect() failed (13: Permission denied)".
;
; The rule allows that one thing and nothing else: a process in httpd_t may send a datagram to a unix
; socket of a service in unconfined_service_t. The permissions of the socket file still apply on top of it.
;
; Install:  sudo semodule -i httpdog-selinux.cil
; Remove:   sudo semodule -r httpdog-selinux
(allow httpd_t unconfined_service_t (unix_dgram_socket (sendto)))
